hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24334","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Malik, meaning Ibn Mighwal, narrated to us, who said: I heard Sayyar Abu al-Hakam more than once narrating from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us, meaning Quba, he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has praised you concerning purification with good, will you not tell me, meaning His saying: In it are men who love to purify themselves, and Allah loves those who purify themselves, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, we find it written upon us in the Torah: cleaning with water."
"24335","Yazid narrated to us, from Sallam ibn Miskin, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, and he mentioned the hadith of the neighbor."
